# The `_imap` stack is the subscription: while it exists, every committed
# client mutation in this tenant's mailboxes (append, copy, move, expunge,
# create, delete, rename; flags only where a mailbox opts in) arrives here
# with @imap.phase == "observe", after the client already got its reply.
# Facts ride under @imap.*: op, mailbox{id,name,role}, dest, uid, objects[]
# {uid, object_key, sha256, flags}, and for an append msg{...} with part
# REFERENCES (sha256) — never bytes. This rule just records what it saw;
# a product would key off @imap.mailbox.role (e.g. "knowledge" → ingest).
WHEN @imap.phase == "observe"
  EMIT ._observed = &object(
         "op", @imap.op,
         "mailbox", @imap.mailbox.name,
         "role", @imap.mailbox.role,
         "uid", @imap.uid)
